                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 86-year-old male patient, admitted on 17/08/2026 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Blood tests revealed mild inflammatory markers. He was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and intravenous fluids for hydration. Clinical response was satisfactory, with improvement in oxygen saturation and dyspnoea. He was discharged on 18/08/2026 in stable condition with oral steroids, inhaled bronchodilators, and instructions for follow-up spirometry. Please continue monitoring his respiratory function and medication compliance. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
